      "Root resorption is a pathological process in which odontoclasts progressively resorb dentin, cementum, or both, with an anatomical distinction of primary clinical importance between internal resorption (originating from the internal surface of the canal, with vital or partially vital pulp sustaining the process) and external resorption (originating from the external surface of the root, typically triggered by damage to the root cementum and overlying periodontal ligament from trauma, excessive orthodontic movement, chronic periapical infection, or intracoronal bleaching procedures with concentrated peroxide).",
